---
import CaseStudy from "../../layouts/CaseStudy.astro";
import Callout from "../../components/Callout.astro";
---

<CaseStudy
  title="Embie — case study — quentin vanderlinden"
  description="A public subsidy platform where citizens and companies file and track requests through their whole lifecycle."
  heading="A public subsidy platform, from request to sign-off"
  crumb="embie"
  tags={["next.js", "trpc", "typescript"]}
  glance={{
    client: "Embie — Brussels",
    year: "2022 – 23",
    duration: "~14 months",
    role: "fullstack — freelance",
  }}
  stack={[
    "react",
    "next.js",
    "typescript",
    "trpc",
    "graphql",
    "state machine",
    "docker",
    "kubernetes",
    "github actions",
    "keycloak",
  ]}
>
  <p>
    For a client of <strong>Embie</strong>, I helped digitalize a subsidies process
    that had been largely manual. The result was a brand-new web platform.
  </p>
  <p>
    Citizens and companies issue subsidy requests for projects abroad and track their
    status throughout the project lifecycle. On the other side, the client's agents
    review requests, ask for modifications, and handle the administrative work around
    them.
  </p>
  <h3>What shipped</h3>
  <p>
    A Next.js application with a typed tRPC API, the request lifecycle modelled as a
    state machine, and auth handled through Keycloak — shipped and run on Kubernetes
    with GitHub Actions.
  </p>
  <Callout tone="info" title="Beyond the code">
    Alongside the build, I helped the team adopt a more agile way of working and
    coached the more junior developers on it.
  </Callout>
  <h3>Result</h3>
  <p>
    One platform replaced a slow, paper-bound process, with a clear, auditable status
    for every request from submission to sign-off.
  </p>
</CaseStudy>
